Z||000008||PaUL||04-27-99||05:37 PM||||as I remember when I still had my computer in my car, the fiero has 3 separate temp sensors, one for the gauge, one for the fan relay, and one for the computer. The fan relay is the single terminal one that looks like a mushroom. Mine wouldnt activate until the engine was real hot, almost boiling over, so I rigged a switch to ground this wire. Its  a hassle to have to remember to switch the fan on. Id rather have a lower temp switch, anyone know where to get these?
Z||000009||EMF||04-27-99||07:21 PM||||yea, that was  my overall plan, to rig a switch to the  fan,  rather than buy a low temp switch. <br>you can  get the low temp switch's in the fiero store, i  noticed, i dont think ill  be shoppin at the fiero store much ,  kinda pricy. they should be in the cooling system section, with the  low temp thermostats and shit. <br>
Z||000010||HF6582||04-27-99||07:43 PM||||i think that summit and jegs carry them.<br>any hypertech dealer can get them.<p>
Z||000011||theogre||04-27-99||09:52 PM||||Why not find out who makes/distributes the "normal" ones available at any pep boys, call the maker, and ask them what parts have the same physical specs as part X, but with a lower temp activation. Or get really friendly with the parts book at you local dealer. Or find a friend at a local dealer who can help......<p>There are only a very few companies that make this junk. They all, Fiero store et al, have to get it from the same people as the normal one. I doubt they actually cost any diferant than the normal one.<p>What you are paying extra is called "Asshole Tax"..... Those of us in the repair business know it all to well. It's what we charge people who are too lazy, incompitent, mean, arrogant,,,,,,,,, to deal with it right in the first place. Fram filter(i think) advertising used to call it "pay me a little now, or pay me <b>alot</b> later!"<p>There are enough smart people here that we should be able to end such a tax on Fiero owners just about completely.<p>Am I saying that all the specialty shops are stiffing us on everything? No. I am saying that spacialty shops are often stiffing you on common items you really could find yourself if you took a bit of time. (<b>You</b> being me, you, and the rest of the Fiero Community.) [[If you think this is a rant, ask me about FOCOA some time. I've shopped thier list.......]]
Z||000012||Shipbuilder||04-29-99||04:16 PM||||To EMF; My 84 4 cyl has 3 temp switches. The one on the thermostat housing feeds the computer. The one mounted vertical on the head feeds the gauge and the temp. light. The one mounted horizontal on the forward side of the head controls the fan. Mine happens to be a two speed fan so the temp. switch has two contacts with different temperature settings. I don't remember what the settings are at the moment, but it cost me $32.00 at the dealer. Good luck
Z||000013||PaUL||04-29-99||04:53 PM||||3 temp switches? didnt I just say that?
